# Example Helm values override — copy to values/mojaloop/mojaloop.yaml.
#
# The path IS the binding: values/<namespace>/<release>.yaml overrides that
# release, merged LAST over the distribution defaults (the file becomes the
# mojaloop-mojaloop-values-override ConfigMap in the HelmRelease's valuesFrom
# chain). Delete this file and the override disappears — presence or absence
# is the complete answer to "does this environment override mojaloop?".
#
# Rules that matter here:
# - Parameters are referenced, never repeated: write ${DOMAIN}, not the
#   literal domain (the hardcoded-literal lint will flag the literal).
# - A file referencing any .env secret key lands as a Secret instead of a
#   ConfigMap, automatically. Everything else must not reference secrets.
# - Lists REPLACE in Helm values. To append to a list the distribution
#   defines, use a patch in patches/ instead of restating the list here.
#
# Example: trim quoting-service replicas on a small environment.
quoting-service:
  replicaCount: 1
